# Shell scripts MUST keep LF in the working tree, on every platform.
#
# With core.autocrlf=true (the Windows default) git rewrites them to CRLF on checkout, and bash
# then reads `set -euo pipefail\r` as an option literally named "pipefail\r":
#
#   01-discover.sh: line 10: set: pipefail
#   : invalid option name
#
# Every cookbook/shell recipe dies at line 1 that way. It is invisible in CI, because
# ubuntu-latest checks out LF regardless, so only a Windows contributor sees it.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same hazard, same reason: these are executed or parsed by tools that reject a stray CR.
*.bash text eol=lf
